# Desktop release updater

Packaged Windows and macOS tools update themselves from GitHub releases. Do not make users re-download from the repo after the first install.

- Keep one version in the package (`__version__`), matching the release tag without the `v`.
- On startup, check `repos/{owner}/{repo}/releases/latest`. Offer an update only when the tag is newer.
- Ship one zip per platform. The file name must contain `windows` or `macos`.
- Ask before installing. Download in the background. A helper waits until the app exits, then replaces the install and relaunches.
- Do not delete `outputs` or saved progress while copying the new build.
- If macOS App Translocation makes the running copy read-only, install the new app under `~/Applications` and open that copy.
- Source checkouts show the release page. They are not overwritten.
- On Windows, the file named `eProContactAudit.exe` is a small launcher. The PyInstaller program is `eProContactAudit-app.exe` beside `_internal`. Running the app from inside the zip extracts only one file, so the launcher tells the user to Extract All.
